cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these policies, please cite this software at the anchor tag
  v0.1.0-rc.1. The Cross-Session Aggregate-Risk Gate implements the model in the
  "Authorized but Composed" position paper listed under references; please cite it
  too when you use that policy.
title: "Agent Governance Policies"
abstract: >-
  MuleSoft Flex/Omni Gateway custom policies (PDK, Rust to WebAssembly) that check
  the authorization integrity of AI agent Model Context Protocol tool calls at a
  gateway enforcement point. Approval-to-Execution Binding checks that the executed
  MCP tools/call is the call an approval record approved. It uses five
  approval-binding-vectors (ABV v0.1) predicates, with HMAC separate-attester and
  single-use checks. The Cross-Session Aggregate-Risk Gate reserves and authorizes
  each call against a shared exposure budget that is keyed on a verified identity.
  It refuses individually valid calls whose total would exceed that budget. This is
  not a compliance certification, and the policies are not production-certified.
type: software
